The Psalter of the 1909 Dominican Breviary (Cormier), vol. 1 pdf 86-245, as data -> psalter1909.json.
Texts from the 1909 OCR (tools/b09/outline_psalter.txt), corrected by hand against the page images and Divinum Officium.
Seasons: adv = Advent ferias/Sundays; pe = after the Epiphany octave to Septuagesima; sept = Septuagesima to Ash Wednesday;
quad = Lent (to Saturday before Passion Sunday); pass = Passiontide (to Wednesday in Holy Week); pasch = Low Sunday to Ascension;
pt = after the octave of Trinity to Advent.  'pa' = pe + sept + pt (per annum).  A missing season key = proper (Proprium de Tempore).
Psalms: integers (Vulgate numbering); '118a'..'118v' = the 22 octonaries of Ps 118 (8 verses each); 30a = Ps 30:2-6;
canticles: 210 Benedicite (O.P. form, no Gloria), 221 Isaiae 12, 222 Ezechiae, 223 Annae, 224 Moysis (Ex 15), 225 Habacuc,
226 Moysis (Deut 32), 231 Benedictus, 232 Magnificat, 233 Nunc dimittis, 234 Quicumque.
A psalm group is [psalms...]; 'Gloria Patri' only at the end of the group (the 1909 rubric: 'Hic non dicitur Gloria Patri').
